- The contract has no constructor. `ToOwner` and `Mining24` are public initializer-like functions and have no access control modifier.
- `ToOwner` sources: `msg.sender`.
  - `msg.sender` reaches `owner`, allowing any caller to replace the owner.
  - `msg.sender` reaches `balances[msg.sender]`, allowing any caller to set their own balance to `totalSupply`.
- `Mining24` sources: `msg.sender`, `_value`, `_minReq`.
  - `msg.sender` reaches `owner`, allowing any caller to replace the owner.
  - `_value` reaches `value`, allowing any caller to set the global `value`.
  - `_minReq` reaches `minReq`, allowing any caller to set the global `minReq`.
